<pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.10" change_id="I3e2dc145530e6b4792797e657bc9d501a6b4c71d" commit="8505e813d2aea2c9befa67d9c43a5ce9803283d9" commit_message="CHROMIUM: video: tegra: host: Support explicit buffer map  Currently nvhost supports only implicit mapping; Data and command buffers are mapped at submit time and command buffers are patches with data buffer addresses. However, this operation is expensive because the command buffers need to be mapped into kernel address space for patching.  This patch adds support to explicit buffer mapping. This allows using the memory addresses direrctly inside command buffers making relocations themselves unnecessary.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:55265 TEST=HW video playback works(along with other patches)  Change-Id: I3e2dc145530e6b4792797e657bc9d501a6b4c71d Signed-off-by: Arto Merilainen &lt;amerilainen@nvidia.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Deepak Nibade &lt;dnibade@nvidia.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Mark Zhang &lt;markz@gpartner-nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/360064 Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="360064" owner_email="markz@gpartner-nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/64/360064/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.10" change_id="Ic284f60b825a5ec37d890050a204103b8e0eedd4" commit="b540bd3e25273d381c5957d33da0453224332a52" commit_message="CHROMIUM: video: tegra: host: add refcounting for vm_buffer  Add refcounting for nvhost_vm_buffer  We get the refcount when 1. buffer is created 2. buffer is re-mapped 3. buffer is pinned  We drop the refcount when 1. buffer is unpinned 2. buffer is unmapped  When refcount goes to zero, we destroy the buffer  Also, do not get VM reference when mapping or pinning the buffers. VM reference should be taken only when channel instance and job are created.  Once channel instance dies and job completes, we will free VM and also free any remaining buffer mapped into it.  Also, add some more comments  BUG=chrome-os-partner:55265 TEST=HW video playback works(along with other patches)  Change-Id: Ic284f60b825a5ec37d890050a204103b8e0eedd4 Signed-off-by: Deepak Nibade &lt;dnibade@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/360065 Commit-Ready: Mark Zhang &lt;markz@gpartner-nvidia.com&gt; Tested-by: Mark Zhang &lt;markz@gpartner-nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="360065" owner_email="markz@gpartner-nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/65/360065/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.10" change_id="I83bf4130ee5e1317f0521412ae362119db0a83e0" commit="2509370de325fd9139bfa0a5d9145bfcd853cbc7" commit_message="CHROMIUM: video: tegra: host: use rb-tree to store buffers  Use rb-tree instead of list to store buffers mapped into each nvhost_vm This should have general advantages of using tree instead of list and hence should help in performance  BUG=chrome-os-partner:55265 TEST=HW video playback works(along with other patches)  Change-Id: I83bf4130ee5e1317f0521412ae362119db0a83e0 Signed-off-by: Deepak Nibade &lt;dnibade@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/360066 Commit-Ready: Mark Zhang &lt;markz@gpartner-nvidia.com&gt; Tested-by: Mark Zhang &lt;markz@gpartner-nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="360066" owner_email="markz@gpartner-nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/66/360066/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.10" change_id="Id8e1aa744e40de2f8dcaeabc8c869e399e0730e6" commit="071e878c40268ee4d3a9547fc33e85ebf8815d23" commit_message="CHROMIUM: video: tegra: host: set error if dma_buf_get fails  Currently if dma_buf_get() fails, we directly jump to error flag and return err which is still zero (success case)  Fix this by setting err to a proper value as below if dma_buf_get() fails err = PTR_ERR(dmabuf);  This will fail the IOCTL and return proper error code to user space  BUG=chrome-os-partner:55265 TEST=HW video playback works(along with other patches)  Change-Id: Id8e1aa744e40de2f8dcaeabc8c869e399e0730e6 Signed-off-by: Deepak Nibade &lt;dnibade@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/360067 Commit-Ready: Mark Zhang &lt;markz@gpartner-nvidia.com&gt; Tested-by: Mark Zhang &lt;markz@gpartner-nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="360067" owner_email="markz@gpartner-nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/67/360067/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I20148591fb231314f1d87bd952a867db02373200" commit="e32187e8da0309635051d12776a33c390c96ae6d" commit_message="chg_st_v2: NVDC: Request max voltage when battery is full.  When the battery indicates that it's full, request the max voltage for the battery.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:54877 BRANCH=None TEST=Verify that EC requests 8688 when battery is full for kevin.  Change-Id: I20148591fb231314f1d87bd952a867db02373200 Signed-off-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/360027 Commit-Ready: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mary Ruthven &lt;mruthven@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="360027" owner_email="aaboagye@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/27/360027/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I0c3abcc2d72e71dd765deade83e0e8cae4498027" commit="ed353cb44ec293a6fedbb21f082d3e7d70299e38" commit_message="bd99955: Update init settings.  - Change fast charging watchdog timer to max. (1020 mins.) - Set charge termination current to 0 mA.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:54877 BRANCH=None TEST=make -j buildall TEST=bd99955 r 0x0f 1; verify upper byte is 0xFF. TEST=bd99955 r 0x17 1; verify is 0.  Change-Id: I0c3abcc2d72e71dd765deade83e0e8cae4498027 Signed-off-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/360147 Commit-Ready: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="360147" owner_email="aaboagye@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/47/360147/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I5e5ca2cdcd4ead383416901c904df1e6fe5a9e28" commit="714c601902c389e9983d12d6a72d5a59e03ad94f" commit_message="bd99955: Make changes for new OTP change.  There's a new OTP change for the BD99955 and therefore the following changes needed to be made.   - Change VFASTCHG_SET1 to 8.704V before CHG_EN is set to 1.  - Change VSYS_REG to 6.144V when starting Fast Charging.  - Change VSYS_REG back to 8.906V when Fast Charge is finished.  - Wait for 50ms to set CHG_EN to off (0) after Fast Charging has ended.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:55220 BUG=chrome-os-partner:55238 BRANCH=None TEST=Flash kevin, plug discharged battery in. Plug AC in. `bd99955 r 0x11 1' and verify that VSYSREG is set to 0x1800 (6144mV). TEST=`bd99955 r 0x1a 1' and verify that VFASTCHARGE is set to 0x2200 (8704mV). TEST=Remove battery. `bd99955 r 0x11 1' and verify that VSYSREG is set to 0x2300 (8960 mV). TEST=Plug in battery and let charge to full. Verify that VSYSREG is set to 0x2300 (8960 mV).  Change-Id: I5e5ca2cdcd4ead383416901c904df1e6fe5a9e28 Signed-off-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/360421 Commit-Ready: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mary Ruthven &lt;mruthven@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="360421" owner_email="aaboagye@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="11" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/21/360421/11" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I05b1fc5348695791ae5c5786b5cb89c94e65b341" commit="4fb8724624bd87582aa1cfe1c8791f02b572288f" commit_message="Gale: make warm_reset work as cold_reset  Cosmos flex cable does not connect warm_reset signal. That makes FAFT to fail. An alias to cold_reset makes both commands to work in the same way.  BUG=b:29587782 TEST=sudo emerge hdctools      sudo servod -b gale &amp;      dut-control warm_reset:on sleep:1 warm_reset:off      Now the DUT resets as expected.  Change-Id: I05b1fc5348695791ae5c5786b5cb89c94e65b341 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/361421 Commit-Ready: Julio Diez &lt;jdiez@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Julio Diez &lt;jdiez@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Todd Broch &lt;tbroch@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="361421" owner_email="jdiez@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/hdctools" project_url="https://chromiu